ClusterShell is an event-based Python library to execute commands in parallel across cluster nodes. Installation and basic configuration defining three node groups (*adm*, *compute*, and *all*) is as follows:

<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
<!-- ohpc_command if [[ ${enable_clustershell} -eq 1 ]];then -->
```bash
# Install ClusterShell
[sms]# {{ install }} clustershell

# Setup node definitions
[sms]# cd /etc/clustershell/groups.d || exit
[sms]# mv local.cfg local.cfg.orig
[sms]# echo "adm: ${sms_name}" > local.cfg
[sms]# echo "compute: ${compute_prefix}[1-${num_computes}]" >> local.cfg
[sms]# echo "all: @adm,@compute" >> local.cfg
```
<!-- ohpc_command fi -->
<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
